# Everything is excluded, and the build inputs are then named.
#
# The usual denylist is written the other way round, and it goes stale the moment somebody adds a
# directory: a `docs/` or a `.env` that nobody remembered to list is silently shipped into the
# build context and, on a careless `COPY`, into the image. An allowlist fails the other way — a
# genuinely new build input makes the build stop, which is the failure worth having.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/

# Re-excluded after the allowlist, because the last matching pattern wins. A local `target/` is
# the single largest thing in this repository and it is useless to the builder, which compiles
# against the pinned toolchain rather than against whatever the host last used.
target/
crates/**/target/

# Working databases. A stray SQLite file in the context is intelligence data being copied into a
# build, which is not something to do by accident.
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
